  "tldr": [
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Prevent cognitive debt by manually retyping LLM-generated code",
      "url": "https://ankursethi.com/blog/prevent-cognitive-debt-by-manually-retyping-llm-generated-code/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49153374",
      "score": 208,
      "comments": 155,
      "author": "mpweiher",
      "published": "2026-08-03T09:32:07Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Blindly accepting LLM code shortcuts deep comprehension, introducing silent logic errors, unvetted dependencies, and severe long-term maintenance overhead.",
        "Manually retyping outputs from tools like GitHub Copilot or Cursor forces line-by-line mental execution and active code review.",
        "Sustainable AI adoption requires balancing generation speed with deliberate developer synthesis to protect code quality and system security."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Retries don't fix eventual consistency",
      "url": "https://var0.xyz/posts/retries-dont-fix-eventual-consistency.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/t0cn1z",
      "score": 9,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "var0xyz",
      "published": "2026-08-03T08:36:37Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Client retries fail against asynchronous replication lag; querying a stale replica repeatedly yields outdated data until state propagation completes.",
        "Enforce strong consistency or sticky session routing to primary nodes when workflows demand immediate read-your-own-writes guarantees.",
        "Design distributed systems using idempotency keys, CRDTs, or saga patterns to handle non-deterministic and out-of-order data propagation safely."
      ]
    },
